VERDICT (q2):
  * H3 NOT reproduced: on the Salam-Sezgin vacuum alpha_SU2 = 2 l_P^2/R^2 (metric, F_(2) and H_(3) contribute equally), not lane F's 3 l_P^2/R^2 (Einstein-Maxwell-Lambda, no H_(3)).
    The 6D reduction reproduces the source's 4D kinetic term exactly (B4b), so the factor is a property of the SUSY theory, not of my method.
  * H4: the 6D U(1) photon is massive (Stueckelberg with B_{theta psi}); only the l = 0 photon was tested here (massive); the source's massless spectrum lists the SU(2) triplet only. N1's alpha_U1 relation has no massless U(1) to apply to.
